      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Swedish unit-linked life assurance (SULZA) rules apply typically when a customer ages 75 or older. The rules wouldn't apply in this scenario since the deceased individual was a UK resident, not Swedish. \n\nThe UK will typically not consider foreign assets, such as those in Spain and the US, when calculating the IHT liability for a UK resident. However, there are potential disclosure obligations and due diligence requirements for the executors to ensure these assets are properly administered and voluntary disclosure can be made to HMRC to mitigate potential IHT liabilities if assets escape detection.",
